Kershaw was born in Dallas, Texas. His father, Don, played for the San Diego Padres in 1984 and 1985. ^{[1]}

## Amateur career

Kershaw attended Highland Park High School in Topeka, Kansas , where he won the Gatorade Player of the Year Award in 2006. As a senior, he went 10-0 with a 0.49 ERA and 123 strikeouts in 62 innings pitched. In his high school career, he was 28-2 with a 0.90 ERA and 350 strikeouts in 175 innings pitched. ^{[ citation needed ]}

Kershaw was drafted by the Colorado Rockies in the 18th round of the 2006 Major League Baseball Draft , but did not sign. Instead, he enrolled at the University of Texas at Arlington to play college baseball for the UT Arlington Mavericks .

